{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob lifted up his feet and went.</b> Since concerning his first journey the Sages said (Sanhedrin 95a) that the earth was contracted for him, and accordingly that journey did not depend on the motion of his feet but on a miracle, it was necessary to state that from this point onward he did not travel by means of the contraction of the earth, but with his feet like any other person."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:52.770177436Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}